.TH JANUSGATE-WEB 8 "July 2026" "JanusGate 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
janusgate-web \- serve the JanusGate HTTPS management interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B janusgate-web
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B janusgate-web --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B janusgate-web
serves static management assets and proxies versioned API requests to
.BR janusgated (8)
over the authenticated local control socket.
The browser interface and the remote automation API use separate HTTPS
listeners on the same configured numeric management address.
The browser listener uses password, optional TOTP, and session authentication;
it never requests a client certificate.
The remote API listener requires both a trusted mapped client certificate and
a compatible bearer token.
No plaintext HTTP listener is provided.
.PP
The service refuses to run as root.
Lifecycle and failure records use the structured JanusGate logging format.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --listen-address " address"
Bind the numeric IPv4 or IPv6 management address.
The default is
.BR 192.168.77.1 .
Wildcard and multicast addresses are rejected.
.TP
.BI --port " port"
Serve the browser interface on the nonzero TCP
.IR port .
The default is 443 on Linux and 8443 on OpenBSD.
.TP
.BI --api-port " port"
Serve the mutual-TLS remote automation API on the distinct nonzero TCP
.IR port .
The default is 9443.
The listener remains disabled until a valid client certification-authority
bundle is installed.
.TP
.BI --certificate " path"
Load the combined PEM certificate and private key at
.IR path .
The default is
.IR /etc/janusgate/certs/server.pem .
.TP
.BI --client-ca " path"
Trust client certificates issued by the root and intermediate certification
authorities in the PEM bundle at
.IR path .
The default is
.IR /etc/janusgate/certs/client-ca.pem .
The service refuses to start if this file exists but is invalid.
.TP
.BI --web-root " path"
Serve static files from the absolute
.IR path .
The default is
.I /usr/share/janusgate/web
on Linux and
.I /usr/local/share/janusgate/web
on OpenBSD.
.TP
.BI --socket " path"
Proxy API requests through the daemon control socket at
.IR path .
The default is
.I /run/janusgate/control/control.sock
on Linux and
.I /var/run/janusgate/control/control.sock
on OpenBSD.
.TP
.B --hsts
Emit HTTP Strict Transport Security after the administrator has established
the intended certificate identity.
.TP
.B --version
Display build version information and exit.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Stop accepting requests and shut down cleanly.
.TP
.B SIGINT
Stop accepting requests and shut down cleanly.
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Validate current TLS material and reload both HTTPS listeners.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/janusgate/certs/server.pem
Default server certificate and private key.
.TP
.I /etc/janusgate/certs/client-ca.pem
Default client certification-authority bundle for the remote API listener.
.TP
.I /usr/share/janusgate/web/
Default immutable web assets on Linux.
.TP
.I /run/janusgate/control/control.sock
Default backend control socket on Linux.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/janusgate/web/
Default immutable web assets on OpenBSD.
.TP
.I /var/run/janusgate/control/control.sock
Default backend control socket on OpenBSD.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The service stopped cleanly or version information was displayed.
.TP
.B 1
Privilege, TLS, listener, backend, or shutdown processing failed.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was invalid.
.SH SECURITY
Use a dedicated unprivileged identity and keep the server PEM private.
Enable HSTS only after confirming that clients trust the permanent
certificate.
The browser listener deliberately does not use mutual TLS.
Remote API requests are accepted only when the client certificate chains to
the configured trust bundle, its leaf fingerprint has an active user or role
mapping, and the bearer token belongs to a compatible principal.
Private, self-hosted, and public certification authorities are supported;
the appliance never accepts a leaf certificate or private key as a trust
anchor.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR janusgatectl (1),
.BR janusgated (8),
.BR janusgate-netd (8)
